			(property "Description" "Resettable Fuse PTC\n\nResettable Fuse. Really a resistor with a postive temperature coefficient who's resistance increases dramatically with an increase in temperature. When heated by the power passing through the resistance rises causing the current to be limited, protecting the circuit. When a PTC cools back down it resumes conducting letting the circuit turn back on."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
